---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import AffiliateLink from "../../components/AffiliateLink.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Zelda: Tears of the Kingdom — Digital or Physical?"
  description="A buying guide for The Legend of Zelda: Tears of the Kingdom on Switch: edition differences, download size, and where to buy cheapest."
>
  <article class="post">
    <h1>Zelda: Tears of the Kingdom — Digital or Physical?</h1>
    <p class="meta">Nintendo Switch · Updated 2026-08-05</p>

    <p>
      <strong>The Legend of Zelda: Tears of the Kingdom</strong> is the 2023
      sequel to Breath of the Wild and one of the most ambitious open-world games
      on Switch. Its headline mechanic — building vehicles and contraptions with
      Zonai devices — gives it hundreds of hours of emergent play.
    </p>

    <h2>Editions available</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Standard physical cartridge</strong> — resellable, no install space needed</li>
      <li><strong>Digital download</strong> — instant, always installed, but a large file (~16 GB + expansion)</li>
      <li><strong>Collector's / Amiibo bundles</strong> — only worth it for collectors</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Digital vs physical: the real trade-off</h2>
    <p>
      There is no "definitive edition" with extra story content, so the choice is
      purely convenience vs resale value. Digital is best if your Switch storage is
      fine and you hate swapping cartridges. Physical wins if you plan to trade it
      in later — Nintendo games hold value unusually well.
    </p>

    <h2>Is the download worth the storage?</h2>
    <p>
      TOTK is a big install. If you're on a 64 GB base Switch, you'll want a microSD
      card regardless. Factor that into the "cheapest" math if you must buy storage
      to fit it.
    </p>

    <h2>Where to buy cheapest</h2>
    <ul class="buy-list">
      <li>
        <AffiliateLink
          network="amazon"
          href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Zelda+Tears+of+the+Kingdom+Switch"
          cta="Check on Amazon"
        />
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="note">
      Prices change frequently — always verify on the store before purchasing.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

